Case 3 : Line EF
If the logical AND result is zero, we cannot immediately decide whether the line is completely
inside or outside the clipping window.
Outcode (E) = 0001
Outcode (F) = 1000
0001 AND 1000 ---- 0000
Since the result of the AND operation is 0000, it means that Line EF is not lying completely on
any one side of the clipping window.
To determine the visible portion, we must find which edge of the clipping window the line
intersects and calculate the intersection point.
The line is then clipped and only the visible portion inside the clipping window is displayed.
Outcodes
Outcode(E) = 0001
Outcode(F) = 1000
Compare the first bit of both outcodes.
The first bit of E is 1 and the first bit of F is 0. It means that E is lying outside the left boundary
of the clipping window. Therefore, the intersection point with the left boundary has to be found.
Let this intersection point be P1.
Now, we have two line segments: EP1 and P1F
Since E is surely outside the clipping window, the line segment EP1 is clipped (discarded).
