The x-coordinate of the intersection point must be X = XL
We have to find the Y-coordinate of the intersection point. We know the equation of a line.
The slope of line AB is : m=y2-y1/x2-x1
Once we know the value of the slope, then we will find the slope between the intersection point P
and one endpoint of the line A. Suppose we want to find the intersection point P for line AB.
Slope of line PA : m = y-y1/x-x1
y-y1=m(x-x1)
y=m(x-x1)+y1
since x=XL
y=m(XL-x1)+y1
We can find the Y-coordinate for point P. Therefore, P = (XL , Y)

Similarly, We Can Find the Intersection Point with the Right Edge
The x-coordinate will be X = XH Therefore,
y=m(XH-x1)+y1
P = (XH , Y)

Similarly, for the Top Boundary
The y-coordinate will be , y = YH
m = y-y1/x-x1
x-x1=(y-y1)/m
x=x1+(y-y1)/m as y=YH

